cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ChartMate in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "ChartMate: publication-ready figures and building-physics indicators from time-series data"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Villa
    given-names: Roberto
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-2900-0774"
    affiliation: "Politecnico di Milano, Department of Architecture, Built Environment and Construction Engineering (DABC)"
    address: "Via Giuseppe Ponzio 31"
    city: Milano
    region: MI
    post-code: "20133"
    country: IT
version: 0.3.1
date-released: 2026-11-19
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/RobertoVilla98/ChartMate"
abstract: >-
  ChartMate is a desktop application for Windows, macOS and Linux that turns
  monitored or simulated time-series data into publication-ready figures and
  building-physics indicators. A pure-Rust engine reads CSV/TSV, Excel, ODS,
  Parquet, HDF5, netCDF-3/4, MATLAB, SAS, SPSS and FITS files as well as MySQL
  queries. The application computes carpet plots, adaptive thermal comfort
  (EN 16798-1, ASHRAE 55), duration curves with exposure doses and ASHRAE
  Guideline 14 calibration indices, exports vector PDF/SVG and 300/600 dpi PNG
  figures at journal column widths, and writes summary statistics as LaTeX
  booktabs, Markdown or TSV tables.
keywords:
  - data visualization
  - time series
  - scientific file formats
  - building physics
  - thermal comfort
  - publication figures
